<section>

<div class="card">
<h3>Fusion 360 (Autodesk)</h3>
<p>Free for students. Industry-level CAD, CAM, and design software.</p>
<a href="https://www.autodesk.com/education" target="_blank">Get Access →</a>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>SOLIDWORKS</h3>
<p>Professional CAD software widely used in engineering industries.</p>
<a href="https://www.solidworks.com" target="_blank">Learn More →</a>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Onshape</h3>
<p>Cloud-based CAD software. No download required.</p>
<a href="https://www.onshape.com/en/" target="_blank">Start →</a>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Lars Christensen (Fusion 360)</h3>
<p>Best YouTube tutorials for Fusion 360 beginners.</p>
<a href="https://www.youtube.com/@cadcamstuff" target="_blank">Watch →</a>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Learn Fusion 360 (Autodesk)</h3>
<p>Official tutorials and guided learning paths.</p>
<a href="https://help.autodesk.com/view/fusion360/ENU/courses/" target="_blank">Start Learning →</a>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>MIT OpenCourseWare (CAD & Design)</h3>
<p>University-level design and engineering courses.</p>
<a href="https://ocw.mit.edu" target="_blank">Explore →</a>
</div>

